    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "# DUNCAN PRIME R02 — TOTAL DEVELOPMENT / SHERIFF / LESTER PROGRAMMING SCHOOL\n\nSTATUS = OWNER-DIRECTED / OSS-FIRST BASE EXECUTION\nPARENT = #206\nBASE_MAIN_AT_START = b18ca6b9cce2dce6fe304ca8ae36c05df4f4dcb1\nPRIME_CORE_MUTATION = NO\nPRODUCTION_MUTATION = NO\nCANON_MUTATION = NO\nAUTO_MERGE = NO\n\n## OWNER GOAL\n\nDUNCAN PRIME develops as the persistent root master-agent. LESTER is DUNCAN PRIME's personal programming assistant. DUNCAN teaches from real evidence; SHERIFF independently tracks discipline and evaluated competence.\n\nLearning loop:\n`REAL ZORR TASK -> EXECUTION -> OBJECTIVE EVAL -> ERROR/SUCCESS CLASSIFICATION -> LESSON -> CHANGED/UNSEEN TRANSFER -> SKILL UPDATE`.\n\n## OWNER-APPROVED ARCHITECTURE — 2026-08-30\n\nApproved exact critical path:\n\n`DUNCAN PRIME -> EXISTING LESTER EXECUTION SURFACE -> INSPECT AI / INSPECT EVALS -> SWE-GYM TASK/EVAL PATTERNS -> EXISTING SHERIFF -> EXISTING PERMANENT ARCHIVE / VERIFIED LESSONS -> DUNCAN PRIME`\n\nPR #217 is SUPERSEDED / CLOSED / NOT MERGED. Its custom programming-school reducer/CLI is not the production path.\n\n## REUSE LAW\n\n`EXISTING ZORR CODE -> NATIVE/STANDARD PLATFORM -> MATURE OSS/UPSTREAM -> MINIMAL ZORR-SPECIFIC GLUE`.\n\nDo not add a second archive, second scheduler, second DB service, generic custom agent framework, custom eval framework, custom scoring engine, or custom training harness while an approved upstream component supplies that function.\n\n## EXISTING ZORR FOUNDATIONS TO REUSE\n\n1. Existing LESTER execution stack and GitHub Actions.\n2. SHERIFF V1: discipline, verdict history, Glicko-2 skill surface, OPA/jsonschema control plane.\n3. Permanent Archive V1 / `zb-archive-v1` RAW evidence.\n4. DUNCAN Fortress R01 fail-closed learning/context.\n5. PR #205 verified-learning/archive patterns: CLOSED SHERIFF verdict -> verified lesson -> deterministic corpus -> task-specific retrieval/policy.\n\n## APPROVED OSS BASE\n\n- Inspect AI: evaluation framework and logs.\n- Inspect Evals: ready evaluation collection including SWE-bench implementation.\n- SWE-Gym: real repository-level training/evaluation task environment and verifier patterns.\n- SWE-smith: future unseen-task factory only after R01; not required for base PASS.\n- mini-swe-agent: future independent control competitor/baseline; not a replacement for LESTER in R01.\n\nAll upstream dependencies/patterns must be pinned/reproducible where practical and license/source verified before adoption.\n\n## R01 BASE-FIRST SCOPE\n\nBuild only the smallest adapter/configuration needed to prove that existing LESTER output can be evaluated through the approved OSS evaluation path and that the resulting durable evidence can flow to existing SHERIFF/Archive without a new ZORR scoring framework.\n\nRequired base behavior:\n- existing LESTER remains the executor;\n- objective eval result comes from upstream eval/test evidence, not a custom ZORR competence reducer;\n- SHERIFF discipline remains separate from competence;\n- one success never promotes a skill to PROVEN;\n- changed/unseen transfer is required for PROVEN/OPERATIONAL-style claims;\n- no fabricated historical scores/backfill;\n- results are auditable and bind exact task/HEAD/evidence;\n- main remains unchanged until a separate merge gate.\n\n## BASE PASS\n\n`LESTER_PROGRAMMING_SCHOOL_OSS_R01 = PASS` only when fresh exact-candidate evidence proves:\n- base is current-main-bound;\n- approved OSS eval component/source/license/ref are explicit;\n- no custom replacement eval/scoring/training framework was added;\n- a deterministic smoke/contract demonstrates existing LESTER -> upstream eval evidence -> SHERIFF/Archive-compatible evidence boundary;\n- changed/unseen-transfer law is represented without fabricated competence;\n- repository validation/full tests pass on exact HEAD;\n- relevant GitHub Actions pass on exact HEAD;\n- fresh GitHub readback matches exact candidate;\n- `MAIN_UNCHANGED=YES` and `MERGED=NO`.\n\nAfter R01 PASS, future slices may add SWE-Gym/SWE-smith task generation and mini-swe-agent league comparison one bounded slice at a time.",
